From: dennitino <alanw6118@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] topaz-0951: touch: read FT5452 frames from register 0x01

On a Redmi Note 12 4G with an aftermarket TFT LCD panel (FT5452 fw 0x32,
vendor 0x48) every frame read from register 0x00 is all zeros and no
contact is ever reported. A bare-metal test from the shim (shim/touchlab.c)
showed the same controller returning real contacts when the read starts at
register 0x01, which is what Android's focaltech_ts_i2c driver does on
every panel. Read 0x01.. into buf + 1 so the parser keeps its layout.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
index 370d18b..ca050c7 100644
--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -478,7 +478,15 @@ touch_focaltech(void)
 	uint8_t buf[63];
 	int x[TOUCH_MAX] = {0}, y[TOUCH_MAX] = {0};
 	uint32_t mask = 0, seen = 0;
-	int err = touch_read(0x38, 0, false, buf, sizeof(buf));
+	/*
+	 * topaz: the FT5452 on aftermarket TFT LCD panels (fw 0x32, vendor 0x48)
+	 * returns all zeros when a read starts at register 0x00, while reads from
+	 * 0x01 carry the touches; Android's focaltech_ts_i2c reads from 0x01
+	 * (gesture id, TD_STATUS, points) on every panel. Read 0x01.. into buf + 1
+	 * so buf[] keeps the classic layout (buf[0], the device mode, is unused).
+	 */
+	buf[0] = 0;
+	int err = touch_read(0x38, 1, false, buf + 1, sizeof(buf) - 1);
 	if (err) {
 		return err;
 	}
